<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Đinh Tiên Hoàng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">924–979</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Dinh Tien Hoang, Đinh Bộ Lĩnh, Dinh Bo Linh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Đinh Tiên Hoàng, born Đinh Bộ Lĩnh, was a local leader from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoa-lu">Hoa Lư</a> who defeated the rival warlords of the Twelve Warlords period. In 968 he proclaimed himself emperor, named the state Đại Cồ Việt and built a fortified capital at Hoa Lư. He was murdered with his eldest son in 979, and the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-dai-hanh">Lê Hoàn</a> soon took the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dinh-tien-hoang.jpg" alt="Đinh Tiên Hoàng" width="298" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hungquoc at Vietnamese Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VuaDinhTienHoang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
